       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. PB164FHOR.
       OPTIONS.
           FLOAT-BINARY DEFAULT IS HIGH-ORDER-RIGHT.
      *> kb/Work PB164 wave 2 - THE FLOAT-BINARY ENDIANNESS PLUMBING,
      *> END TO END. 11.9.8.3 SR3: THE CLAUSE'S HIGH-ORDER-RIGHT IS
      *> IMPLIED FOR EVERY STANDARD BINARY FLOAT ITEM WITHOUT ITS OWN
      *> ENDIANNESS-PHRASE; 13.18.60.4 GR19b: HIGH-ORDER-RIGHT MEANS
      *> LITTLE-ENDIAN. SO B32'S IMAGE OF 1.5 (BINARY32 BITS 3FC00000)
      *> IS THE BYTE SEQUENCE 00 00 C0 3F. A ROUND-TRIP GOLDEN CANNOT
      *> SEE BYTE ORDER (BOTH LANES WOULD REVERSE - SELF-INVERSE), SO
      *> THE DISCRIMINATING LEG READS SINGLE BYTES OF THE IMAGE WITH
      *> FUNCTION ORD (15.70 - ORDINAL POSITION, NATIVELY BYTE + 1):
      *> ORD OF BYTE 1 = 1 (0x00) AND OF BYTE 4 = 64 (0x3F) - UNDER
      *> THE DEFAULT HIGH-ORDER-LEFT THOSE WOULD BE 64 AND 1. COMP-1
      *> IN THE SAME GROUP STAYS BIG-ENDIAN (GR13/GR21 IMPLEMENTOR
      *> PIN; GR19c SCOPES THE CLAUSE TO THE STANDARD USAGES): ORD OF
      *> ITS BYTE 1 = 64 (0x3F). THE ROUND-TRIP LEG THEN PROVES THE
      *> PARSE LANE INVERTS UNDER THE SAME IMPLIED PHRASE.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 GH.
          05 B32 USAGE FLOAT-BINARY-32 VALUE 1.5.
          05 B64 USAGE FLOAT-BINARY-64 VALUE -2.25.
          05 C1 USAGE COMP-1 VALUE 1.5.
       01 GH2.
          05 B32-2 USAGE FLOAT-BINARY-32.
          05 B64-2 USAGE FLOAT-BINARY-64.
          05 C1-2 USAGE COMP-1.
       01 XH PIC X(16).
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
           MOVE GH TO XH
      *> B32 IMAGE = BYTES 1-4; LITTLE-ENDIAN 1.5f = 00 00 C0 3F.
           DISPLAY "B32=[" FUNCTION ORD(XH(1:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(XH(4:1)) "]"
      *> B64 IMAGE = BYTES 5-12; LITTLE-ENDIAN -2.25 = 00 x6, 02, C0.
           DISPLAY "B64=[" FUNCTION ORD(XH(5:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(XH(11:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(XH(12:1)) "]"
      *> COMP-1 IMAGE = BYTES 13-16; STAYS BIG-ENDIAN: 3F C0 00 00.
           DISPLAY "C1 =[" FUNCTION ORD(XH(13:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(XH(16:1)) "]"
           MOVE XH TO GH2
           DISPLAY "RT =[" B32-2 " " B64-2 " " C1-2 "]"
           STOP RUN.
